  "suite": "cores",
  "description": "One ROM, many core stacks. This is the manifest that makes a CORE regression visible rather than a ROM regression: every case below runs the identical ROM for the identical number of frames, so any hash that moves points straight at the core that differs. Measured relationships on the day these goldens were recorded (2026-09-03) - if one of these stops holding, that IS the finding: (a) FIX/FIX/FIX differs from FMC/FMC/FMC; (b) on this ROM the difference is entirely the PPU - swapping only CPU_FMC->CPU_FIX or only APU_FMC->APU_FIX leaves the framebuffer byte-identical, while swapping only PPU_FMC->PPU_FIX reproduces the full FIX/FIX/FIX hash; (c) each gimmick PPU (LQ, ULQ, BFR) produces its own distinct hash, which is what locks its 'personality' in place.",
  "roots": {
    "story": "Windows/bin/Release/net10.0-windows/win-x64/Data/story"
  },
